# Looker Studio Database Specification: GCP-SMART-IOT-ANALYTICS-PLATFORM

This document defines the schema and connection settings for the Looker Studio 
Dashboard, sourcing data from the BigQuery analytics layer.

## 1. Data Source Configuration
* **Connector:** Google BigQuery (Native)
* **Project ID:** `${var.project_id}`
* **Dataset ID:** `iot_analytics_ds`
* **Table ID:** `enriched_telemetry`
* **Data Refresh Rate:** 15 Minutes (Standard) / 1 Minute (Premium)

## 2. Table Schema & Field Mapping

| Field Name     | Data Type     | Default Aggregation | Role              |
| :------------- | :------------ | :------------------ | :---------------- |
| `timestamp`    | Date & Time   | None                | Primary Dimension |
| `device_id`    | Text          | None                | Break Dimension   |
| `temperature`  | Number        | Average             | Metric            |
| `humidity`     | Number        | Average             | Metric            |
| `alert_level`  | Text          | None                | Filter Dimension  |
| `region`       | Geo (Alpha-2) | None                | Map Dimension     |
| `processed_at` | Date & Time   | None                | Metadata          |

## 3. Calculated Fields (Virtual Schema)

To add "Smart" logic at the reporting layer, create these fields in Looker Studio:

### A. Ingestion Latency (ms)
```sql
DATETIME_DIFF(processed_at, timestamp, SECOND)